lls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Tennessee enters the 2028 presidential race as one of the most Republican-leaning states in the country, with a partisan lean of roughly fourteen points toward the GOP and recent presidential results that ran well beyond that. The incumbent president is term-limited, so neither side carries an incumbency advantage, and no candidate-specific polling or expert ratings are available for the general election.\n\nThe forecast therefore rests on the state's fundamentals. Reports in 2026 that President Trump's approval had slipped below 50 percent in Tennessee hint at some room for Democrats, but that signal is dated and modest against the state's durable Republican margin. The Republican nominee is clearly favored, and the wide uncertainty reflects how little race-specific information exists this far before the election.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0603, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1012, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.11, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1055, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0961, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1038, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0969, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1086, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.082, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0965, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1008, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0993, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0988, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1057, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0921, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0979, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.104, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0893, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.08, "margin"